# Cargo build output — every workspace has its own `target/` (root, xyscript-gui, pdf-spike).
# These are large (hundreds of MB to GB) and rebuilt from source, so they never go in git.
target/

# The shipped Windows binary is a build artifact — CI rebuilds it for every platform.
# Delete this line if you'd rather track dist/xyscript.exe in the repo (note: it's ~78 MB,
# and GitHub warns on files over 50 MB).
dist/

# CI binaries pulled down with `gh run download` — each artifact lands in its own folder named
# after the artifact. They run 78-170 MB each, and GitHub REJECTS any file over 100 MB, so these
# must never be committed. Tip: download into one folder instead — `gh run download -D artifacts`.
/artifacts/
/xyscript-linux-x86_64/
/xyscript-macos-universal/
/xyscript-windows-x86_64.exe/

# Claude Code's per-machine local settings (permission allowlists etc.) — not shared state.
# A shared `.claude/settings.json` would still be tracked if one is ever added.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Personal experimental script kept in the repo root — not part of the project.
/savesess.xpl

# Debug symbols and OS cruft.
*.pdb
Thumbs.db
